{"repositoryId":140485992,"availability":"available","full":"felipemarcos/cabelo","name":"cabelo","description":"Parallax scrolling animation library","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2018-07-10T20:50:47Z","updated":"2026-10-18T21:09:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://felipemarcos.github.io/cabelo/","topics":["animation","parallax","scrolling"],"demo":"https://felipemarcos.github.io/cabelo/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:03.397Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:03.397Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:03.397Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T09:34:03.397Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Tiny, dependency-free library to animate anything based on the scroll position.","Cabelo turns the scroll position into a timeline. You describe what a property should look like at given scroll positions, and cabelo interpolates everything in between as the page scrolls, up and down, as fast as the user likes."],"features":["Anything is animatable: transforms, CSS properties, CSS variables, colors, SVG attributes, DOM properties like textContent, and plain JavaScript objects.","Positions in pixels or relative to elements: 'top-bottom' means \"when the top of the element reaches the bottom of the viewport\", and is measured again when the layout changes.","Predictable: overlapping tweens resolve the same way no matter how fast you scroll, so jumping around the page never leaves stale values behind.","Keyframes, easing, staggering: multiple positions per tween, CSS-like easings (cubic-bezier(), steps()), and per-target function values.","Hooks: run code or toggle classes when the scroll position crosses a point or enters a range."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/felipemarcos/cabelo/blob/master/readme.md","fingerprint":"718205d6d0a9281e7b9ed0a753bedcfdf79223f383e513d7cf976276cc49364f","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T09:34:0